    "result_text": "The full test suite is just the one acceptance test class (the other two files are a base class and a helper), and it passes. `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule and made the suite green.\n\n**The rule:** `membershipTier` becomes `GOLD` when the owner's household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3+ members after the create; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\n**Key design decision:** GOLD is a *read-time household aggregate* \u2014 it depends on how many owners currently share the `householdId`, which grows as members are added after an owner is created. The existing `bulkSignupWarning` flag is the same shape (a `findAllOwners()` aggregate applied to the DTO in the controller after mapping), so I followed that established pattern rather than pushing repository access into the MapStruct mapper. This leaves the mapper's SILVER/BRONZE logic untouched and applies GOLD as an overriding tier.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 in `toOwnerDtoWithBulkWarning` (the central mapping method used by `getOwner`, `addOwner`, and `listOwners`), after mapping the DTO, promote to `GOLD` when the household has \u2265 3 members. Added a `GOLD_HOUSEHOLD_MEMBER_THRESHOLD` constant and a `householdMemberCount(householdId)` helper that counts owners sharing the id (returning 0 for a null/blank id, i.e. non-household owners).\n\n2. `openapi.yml` \u2014 added `GOLD` to the `membershipTier` enum (the DTO field is a generated `MembershipTierEnum`, so GOLD had to be a valid enum value) and updated the field description.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` builds a 3-member shared household and reads the third owner back as GOLD \u2014 it now passes, and existing SILVER/BRONZE behavior is unchanged since those still flow through the mapper untouched.",
